hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16754","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from his maternal uncle Musafi, from Safiyya daughter of Shayba, mother of Mansur, she said: A woman from Banu Sulaym who delivered most of the people of our house informed me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Uthman ibn Talha, and once he said: She asked Uthman ibn Talha why the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called you; he said: I had seen the two horns of the ram when I entered the House, and I forgot to order you to cover them, so cover them, for it should not be in the House anything that occupies one praying; Sufyan said: The two horns of the ram remained in the House until the House burned and they burned."
